  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in Montana through FY2026 to date shows concentrated activity in a few agencies, industries, and vendors. The federal government obligated $896M in the state, across 5,839 awards, with an average award size of $153K. Obligations fell 21.8% year over year. The Department of Defense, Department of Agriculture, and Department of Homeland Security are the largest buyers, with obligations of $316M, $204M, and $169M respectively. Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance, Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction lead industry spending at $137M, $122M, and $119M respectively. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC, ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV, and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. are the top vendors by dollars obligated, with $135M, $58.8M, and $57M respectively. Recent fiscal history shows growth into FY24 and FY25 followed by a pullback in FY26 to date: FY21 was $691M, FY22 was $925M, FY23 was $1B, FY24 was $1.1B, FY25 was $1.1B, and FY26 is $896M. Use these figures to prioritize agency targets, industry positioning, or partner selection for Montana federal opportunities.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Montana changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 21.8% year over year. Fiscal history shows obligations rising from $691M in FY21 to $1.1B in FY24 and FY25, then pulling back to $896M in FY26 to date. The state has 5,839 awards so far in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $153K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are driving Montana federal spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $316M, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $204M and the Department of Homeland Security at $169M. Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance leads industries at $137M, followed by Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $122M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $119M. Agencies and those three industries together account for a large share of FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
